    {
      "id": "long-hall",
      "name": "The Long Hall",
      "description": "A long, low hall lit by a row of lamps hanging from the roof. There are doors all round it, but they are all locked, and in the middle stands a little three-legged table made of solid glass, with a tiny golden key and a bottle labelled DRINK ME upon it. The air is hot and the floor is damp, as if someone has been crying gallons of tears. The rabbit-hole lies west, a thick wood is east, and behind a low curtain to the south a little door opens on the loveliest garden you ever saw.",
      "exits": {
        "n": null,
        "e": "mushroom-wood",
        "s": "croquet-ground",
        "w": "rabbit-hole"
