    {
      "id": "tea-party",
      "name": "The Mad Tea-Party",
      "description": "A table is set out under a tree in front of the March Hare's house, laid for a great many more than three. The Hatter and the March Hare are having tea at one corner, using a sleeping Dormouse as a cushion, and the Hatter's watch tells the day of the month but not what o'clock it is. It is always six o'clock here, so it is always tea-time, and nobody has time to wash the things between whiles. The wood with the great mushroom lies west.",
