    {
      "id": "croquet-ground",
      "name": "The Queen's Croquet-Ground",
      "description": "The beautiful garden at last, with bright flower-beds and cool fountains. Near the entrance stands a large rose-tree whose white roses three gardeners are hastily painting red before the Queen comes. The croquet-ground itself is all ridges and furrows, the balls are live hedgehogs, the mallets live flamingoes, and the soldiers double themselves up to make the arches. The little door back into the long hall is north; the court of justice is south.",
